Z||000000||wvhdls||05-21-2001||01:58 PM||||HELP! I recently bought an 86GT that was missing both headlight relays (left and right) among other things. I have put in the correct relays (including the isolation one), replaced the driver's side motor, and studied hard. Now, when I turn on the lights, the passenger side works right, but the driver's side does the opposite thing... it goes down when it's supposed to go up and etc. Can this easily be fixed, or should I just duct tape two flashlights on the front?<BR>I'm almost buggy by now.||||reg||8
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||05-21-2001||02:47 PM||||Cheesey answer here, but, have you tried reversing the wires to the headlight motor? if it goes down when it should go up, and vice-a-verca&lt;sp??&gt; the a quick 'McGyver' fix would just be to switch the positive/negative lines to the motor, throw some black tape over the splices and call it a day.||||reg||1
